 for establishing the existence of a solution to the following system of equations:
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
-\Delta u = \lambda f(u) + \mu g(v) & \text{in } \Omega, \\
-\Delta v = \lambda f(v) + \mu g(u) & \text{in } \Omega, \\
u = v = 0 & \text{on } \partial\Omega,
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where $\Omega$ is a bounded domain in $\mathbb{R}^N$ with a smooth boundary, and $\lambda$ and $\mu$ are positive constants. The functions $f$ and $g$ are continuous and satisfy the condition $f(s)g(s) > 0$ for all $s \neq 0$. The first proof utilizes the Leray-Schauder degree theory, while the second proof employs the fixed point theorem of Krasnoselskii.
